name: Operator status keeps a real repository index distinct from accepted Map context
size: 240x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operator_status.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | commands
expect: Commands
expect: Desktop alerts unavailable
expect-not: shell route
expect-not: focus unknown
submit: run context:build {"sampleLimit":20,"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 run receipt | index-produced
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 repo index ready | wide-index-ready
expect-not: ctx:not built
expect-not: repo index not built
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operator_status.py @TMP_TARGET @ART built
type: status-copy draft
resize: 160x48
live-snap: index-160x48
expect: status-copy draft
resize: 96x89
live-snap: index-96x89
expect: status-copy draft
resize: 80x24
live-snap: index-80x24
expect: status-copy draft
resize: 60x20
live-snap: index-60x20
expect: status-copy draft
resize: 40x12
live-snap: index-40x12
expect: status-copy draft
ask: Do the status labels distinguish commands, desktop alerts and the optional repository index, while keeping the unsent draft and leaving Map unaccepted across the viewport matrix?
keys: C-u
resize: 120x36
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI VIZ | gallery
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 COMPONENT STACK | components
expect: 2 manifests · 1 lockfile
expect-not: 1 lockfiles
expect: declared ^1.0
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
keys: Escape
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
resize: 240x36
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 repo index ready | recovered-index
expect: Commands
expect-not: repo index not built
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operator_status.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does restart retain the same real index and one auxiliary run, with correct dependency-count grammar and no model work, scan jobs or accepted Map?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
